# A string test asked of a column that holds numbers. The error is the SCALAR
# KERNEL'S OWN sentence, and it names no row: every row fails identically, so the
# column is what is wrong and "at row 0" would send you to look at blameless data.
df = dataframe({n: [1, 2, 3]})
print(df.where(@n.starts_with("a")).count())
